// The fixtures themselves are generated by scripts/build_fixtures.py
// (`make fixtures`); never hand-edit them. Every file in data/fixtures is
// imported statically here, so a missing or renamed fixture fails `npm run build`.
//
// Type checking, in two layers:
// 1. Compile time: each import goes through `typed<T>()`, whose parameter is
//    `Widen<T>` (T with string-literal enums widened to string, tuples to arrays).
//    TypeScript infers JSON imports with plain `string`/`number[]`, so this is
//    the strictest structural check possible: a missing or mistyped key fails
//    the build. Nothing narrower than `string` can be checked this way.
// 2. Runtime: `checkFixtures()` checks every enum-typed field against the value
//    lists in ./types and that every file named in index.json is imported here.

